Author: Hongjie Jiang [aut], Anchi Che [aut], Yanxiao Han [aut] (co-corresponding author), Yanshuo Han [aut, cre] (co-corresponding author)
Maintainer: Yanshuo Han <yanshuohan@dlut.edu.cn>
Description: Differential analysis for two-group bulk RNA-seq based on
    Generalized Gamma (GG) modeling and information-geometric natural-gradient
    estimation. The inferential core fits gene-wise GG models, applies TMM
    preprocessing, limma-style fitFDist variance shrinkage, moderated-t
    testing for primary DE, and additional diagnostic channels for GG mean,
    manifold distance, differential variability (DV), and differential shape
    (DG). The package reports DD via Cauchy combination of DV and DG-gamma,
    SGCB_Score via Cauchy combination of DE and DD, optional calibrated
    bootstrap uncertainty columns, and deployment wrappers for
    contrast-defined or pairwise follow-up from richer study designs.
